<!--
     Copyright (C) 2026 The LineageOS Project
     SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

     JamesDSP (james.dsp, root flavor) is the ROM's audio-effect controller in place of AudioFX.
     AudioFX is privileged, platform-signed and persistent, so it is never background-restricted;
     JamesDSP is a plain product app and needs both entries below to do the same job.

     initial-package-state: config_stopSystemPackagesByDefault is true, so a preinstalled app starts
     STOPPED on a fresh /data and receives no broadcasts; no BOOT_COMPLETED, no
     OPEN_AUDIO_EFFECT_CONTROL_SESSION; and the DSP stays off until the user opens the app (measured
     on build 19 after a clean flash: stopped=true, no process, no service). LineageOS exempts its own
     apps the same way (initial-package-stopped-states-*.xml), as does rs4-microg for microG/Aurora.

     allow-in-power-save: the state JamesDSP's root flavor asks the user for itself
     (REQUEST_IGNORE_BATTERY_OPTIMIZATIONS; MainActivity: "require battery optimizations turned off ...
     otherwise, the service will be block from launching from background"). Without it the service's
     first foreground starts at boot are refused (ForegroundServiceStartNotAllowedException) until
     BOOT_COMPLETED's temporary allowance. Operator's decision (2026-11-16): pre-grant it in the ROM.
-->
<config>
    <initial-package-state package="james.dsp" stopped="false" />
    <allow-in-power-save package="james.dsp" />
</config>
